  "$comment": "Curation manifest for the @qball-inc/react icon system. Single source of truth for scripts/generate-icons.mjs and the icons contract test. `name` is the CANONICAL kebab id (the registry key + the base of the PascalCase export). `track` is `ui` (default), `ai`, or `brand`. `source` is `lucide` (default — codegen from lucide-react `__iconNode`), `authored` (hand-committed original-art .tsx, NOT generated), or `asset` (hand-committed converted brand asset). `lucideName` overrides the lucide id to pull geometry FROM when it differs from `name` (e.g. `ai-sparkle` <- lucide `sparkles`). `alias` records a friendly lucide alias-stub name re-exported as a named alias + keyed in the registry (e.g. filter -> funnel). `exportName` overrides the default PascalCase named export when it would collide with an existing non-icon component (e.g. the `search` icon vs the Search input primitive). `category` is organizational only (it groups the gallery; it is NOT a name prefix). AC-4 registry split: the UI + AI tracks own the dynamic `<Icon name>` registry + the canonical `IconName` union; brand marks are PascalCase named exports under their own `BrandIconName` union (NOT in the icon registry). WP-B-4b.2-B1 shipped a 22-icon UI slice; WP-B-4b.2-B2 expands UI to the full 76 (§8) and adds the AI + Brand tracks. Every shipped name is a 1.0 stability contract (§11).",
